LEC 05 List expression:

1. empty list:
    empty is not same as no list!

    empty -> empty list

2. create list:
    use 'cons' keyword to add item into a list

    EX. (cons 'bread empty) ;; cons constructs a list by adding an item to the front of another list

    Ex. (cons 'hello
            (cons 'world
                (cons 'ok empty))) 

    use 'rest' keyword to erase some item of the list

    Ex. (cons 'hello
            (rest (cons 'world
                    (cons 'ok empty)))) -> output: (cons 'hello (cons 'ok empty))

    use 'first' keyword return the first item of the list 

    Ex. (first (cons 'hello
                    (cons 'world
                        cons 'ok empty))) -> output: 'hello

3. empty?
    empty? can be used for testing whether a list is empty or not

4. list of racket list operations
    cons - constructs a list from a value and a list by adding the value to the front
    first - consumes a non-empty list and produces the first value in the list 
    rest - consumes a non-empty list and produces a list with the first 
    empty? - consumes any and produces true if the value is empty (Any -> Bool)
    list? - consumes any and produces true if the value is a list
    cons? - consumes any and produces true if the value is a non-empty list




